From: nuubOS <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] nuubOS CHEEVOS_HARDCORE_SET command

nuubOS lets a user flip RetroAchievements Hardcore Mode mid-session
from its own in-game Quick Menu (nuubos-emud drives RetroArch on the
stdin command interface, as with CHEATS_LOAD/NETPLAY_STOP).

- CHEEVOS_HARDCORE_SET <0|1>: sets cheevos_hardcore_mode_enable and
  applies it live the same way RetroArch's own menu checkbox does
  (rcheevos_hardcore_enabled_changed, not the one-directional "pause"
  path used by the CHEEVOS_HARDCORE_MODE_TOGGLE command/hotkey, which
  only turns hardcore off and only when the setting is already on),
  then resets the content: neither the menu checkbox nor the existing
  toggle command do that on their own, and nuubOS wants a clean game
  state on either side of the switch. Replies
  "CHEEVOS_HARDCORE_SET OK|FAILED".

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [nuubOS session manager integration]
---
--- a/command.c
+++ b/command.c
@@ -911,6 +911,36 @@
    return ret;
 }
 
+/* nuubOS: sets RetroArch's own Hardcore Mode setting live (same write
+ * path as its menu checkbox) and resets the content either way, since
+ * neither the checkbox nor CMD_EVENT_CHEEVOS_HARDCORE_MODE_TOGGLE do
+ * that on their own. Replies "CHEEVOS_HARDCORE_SET OK|FAILED". */
+bool command_cheevos_hardcore_set(command_t *cmd, const char *arg)
+{
+   char reply[64];
+   size_t _len;
+   bool ret = false;
+
+#ifdef HAVE_CHEEVOS
+   {
+      settings_t *settings = config_get_ptr();
+      bool want            = !string_is_empty(arg) && arg[0] == '1';
+
+      if (settings->bools.cheevos_hardcore_mode_enable != want)
+      {
+         settings->bools.cheevos_hardcore_mode_enable = want;
+         rcheevos_hardcore_enabled_changed();
+      }
+      command_event(CMD_EVENT_RESET, NULL);
+      ret = true;
+   }
+#endif
+   _len = snprintf(reply, sizeof(reply), "CHEEVOS_HARDCORE_SET %s\n",
+         ret ? "OK" : "FAILED");
+   cmd->replier(cmd, reply, _len);
+   return ret;
+}
+
